  {
   "kind": "assistant",
   "reply": {
    "message": "Automatic watering needs two parts: a soil moisture sensor that tells the board how dry the soil is, and something that actually moves water when it's dry. I found good options for both. The sensor side is simple (a capacitive moisture probe reads fine at the Pico's 3.3 V), but how you get water to the plant changes the wiring a lot, so I put two common setups side by side - pick one and I'll build the full wiring for it.\n\nHow does the water get to the plant?",
