   "kind": "assistant",
   "reply": {
    "message": "Here's the plan: a capacitive soil moisture probe (GP26, which is ADC0) tells the Pico how wet the soil is, and a logic-level MOSFET module (GP15) switches the mini pump on when it's dry. The pump and MOSFET module get their power from VBUS (the 5 V USB line), since the pump needs more current than a GPIO can give. Nothing is wired on the board yet — press Apply on the card to write it. One thing to buy: a flyback diode (e.g. 1N4007) across the pump, stripe toward the + wire, to protect the MOSFET when the pump switches off. After you apply it, I can write starter code that reads the sensor and turns the pump on below a threshold you set.",
    "confidence": "documented",
